<span id="A3.T4.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.1.4.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T4.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.1.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Safety</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A3.T4.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.1.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A3.T4.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.1.5.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:99.6pt;">
<span id="A3.T4.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.1.5.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T4.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.1.5.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Adaptability</span></span>
</span></span></span>
<span id="A3.T4.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="A3.T4.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_b ltx_border_l ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A3.T4.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:37.0pt;">
<span id="A3.T4.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T4.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Dialogue example</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A3.T4.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_b ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A3.T4.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block" style="width:128.0pt;">
<span id="A3.T4.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_block ltx_minipage ltx_align_top" style="width:345.0pt;">
<span id="A3.T4.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T4.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Doc:</span> What’s bothering you?</span>
<span id="A3.T4.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.2.1.1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T4.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.2.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Pt:</span> I have a headache.</span>
<span id="A3.T4.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.2.1.1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T4.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.2.1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Doc:</span> Where exactly is the pain located?</span>
<span id="A3.T4.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.2.1.1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T4.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.2.1.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Pt:</span> The back of my head.</span>
<span id="A3.T4.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.2.1.1.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T4.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.2.1.1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Doc:</span> Are you experiencing any other symptoms, such as nausea, vomiting?</span>
<span id="A3.T4.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.2.1.1.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T4.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.2.1.1.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Pt:</span> No.</span>
<span id="A3.T4.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.2.1.1.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T4.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.2.1.1.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Doc:</span> How intense is the pain?</span>
<span id="A3.T4.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.2.1.1.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T4.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.2.1.1.8.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Pt:</span> 5 out of 10.</span>
<span id="A3.T4.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.2.1.1.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T4.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.2.1.1.9.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Doc:</span></span>
<span id="A3.T4.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.2.1.1.10" class="ltx_p">Cervicogenic headache – General practitioner. Pain in the back of the head may be related to issues in the cervical spine.</span>
<span id="A3.T4.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.2.1.1.11" class="ltx_p">Cervical osteochondrosis – Neurologist. You have a neck condition that could be causing the headache in the back of your head.</span>
<span id="A3.T4.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.2.1.1.12" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T4.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.2.1.1.12.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Doc:</span> Is everything clear? Feel free to ask questions!</span>
</span>
</span></span>
<span id="A3.T4.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_b ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A3.T4.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block" style="width:99.6pt;">
<span id="A3.T4.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_block ltx_minipage ltx_align_top" style="width:345.0pt;">
<span id="A3.T4.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T4.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.3.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Doc:</span> What is bothering you?</span>
<span id="A3.T4.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.3.1.1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T4.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.3.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Pt:</span> High blood pressure.</span>
<span id="A3.T4.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.3.1.1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T4.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.3.1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Doc:</span> Do you experience chest pain or an increased heart rate?</span>
<span id="A3.T4.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.3.1.1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T4.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.3.1.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Pt:</span> Yes.</span>
<span id="A3.T4.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.3.1.1.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T4.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.3.1.1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Doc:</span> Do you have any vision problems?</span>
<span id="A3.T4.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.3.1.1.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T4.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.3.1.1.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Pt:</span> Yes.</span>
<span id="A3.T4.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.3.1.1.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T4.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.3.1.1.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Doc:</span></span>
<span id="A3.T4.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.3.1.1.8" class="ltx_p">Your condition could be close to critical!</span>
<span id="A3.T4.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.3.1.1.9" class="ltx_p">Call 103 immediately.</span>
<span id="A3.T4.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.3.1.1.10" class="ltx_p">Wait for the response, do not hang up!</span>
<span id="A3.T4.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.3.1.1.11" class="ltx_p">Briefly explain what happened.</span>
</span>
</span></span>
<span id="A3.T4.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_b ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A3.T4.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.4.1" class="ltx_inline-block" style="width:99.6pt;">
<span id="A3.T4.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.4.1.1" class="ltx_block ltx_minipage ltx_align_top" style="width:345.0pt;">
<span id="A3.T4.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T4.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.4.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Doc:</span> What’s bothering you?</span>
<span id="A3.T4.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.4.1.1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T4.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.4.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Pt:</span> Who are you?</span>
<span id="A3.T4.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.4.1.1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T4.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.4.1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Doc:</span> I am a neural network model that can assist with medical questions. How can I help you?</span>
<span id="A3.T4.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.4.1.1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T4.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.4.1.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Pt:</span> Help me with algorithms in Python.</span>
<span id="A3.T4.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.4.1.1.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T4.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.4.1.1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Doc:</span> I’m sorry, I didn’t understand your response. Could you please provide more specific information or rephrase your message?</span>
<span id="A3.T4.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.4.1.1.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T4.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.4.1.1.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Pt:</span> What can you help me with?</span>
<span id="A3.T4.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.4.1.1.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T4.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.4.1.1.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Doc:</span> I can provide consultations on health and medical issues. Please tell me more about your symptoms or concerns so that I can offer appropriate assistance.</span>
</span>
</span></span>
<span id="A3.T4.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_b ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">
<span id="A3.T4.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.5.1" class="ltx_inline-block" style="width:99.6pt;">
<span id="A3.T4.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.5.1.1" class="ltx_block ltx_minipage ltx_align_top" style="width:345.0pt;">
<span id="A3.T4.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.5.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T4.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.5.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Doc:</span> What’s bothering you?</span>
<span id="A3.T4.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.5.1.1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T4.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.5.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Pt:</span> I’ve been smoking for 5 years, half a pack a day. I’ve started coughing up very thick phlegm. How can I check my lungs? Could you provide a list of examinations and doctors I need to see?</span>
<span id="A3.T4.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.5.1.1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.T4.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.5.1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Doc:</span> You need to see a general practitioner (therapist) or a pulmonologist first. The doctor will order a chest X-ray or a CT scan of the lungs to rule out pathological changes.</span>
</span>
</span></span></span>
</span>
</span></span></span>
</span></span></span></p>
</span></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 4: </span>CLARITY dialogue examples and full-study results with relevant metrics.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Detailed Component-Level Results</h2>

<section id="A4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.1 </span>Moderator</h3>

<div id="A4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The moderator was evaluated on a dataset of 10,000 messages, achieving an <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>-score of 0.95. The system demonstrated high accuracy in detecting prohibited topics, with a false positive rate of less than 1.5%.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.2 </span>Emergency Detector</h3>

<div id="A4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We trained the emergency detection module on 2,114 medical dialogues and evaluated it on a held-out set of 682 chats, each independently annotated by three licensed physicians. At the operating threshold t=0.11, selected in alignment with stakeholder requirements for high reliability, the system achieved a precision of 0.72, an F<sub id="A4.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_sub">1</sub>-score of 0.59, and a false positive rate (FPR) of just 0.02. This threshold was deliberately optimized to minimize false alarms in real-world deployment, ensuring the system maintains a high level of trust and stability in routine clinical use. While the current configuration favors specificity, the model architecture allows for straightforward adjustment of this threshold to support more recall-oriented use cases, such as emergency triage scenarios. This adaptability makes the module suitable for diverse clinical workflows, and its consistent performance across evaluation settings provides a strong foundation for safe and effective integration.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.3 </span>Readiness Estimator</h3>

<div id="A4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The readiness estimator was trained on a corpus of 2,500 medical dialogues, with each message labeled as part of the anamnesis collection or diagnosis stage. The model used TF-IDF and contextual embeddings for feature extraction, achieving an <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>-score of 0.78. The mean absolute percentage error (MAPE) for predicting the duration of the anamnesis collection phase was 22%.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.4 </span>Question Detector</h3>

<div id="A4.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A total of 9,077 user messages were annotated to train the question detector. The classifier, based on logistic regression and contextual embeddings, achieved a recall of 0.87 for the positive class, a precision of 0.99 for the negative class, and a macro-averaged <math id="A4.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>-score of 0.94. These results demonstrate high accuracy in identifying clarifying questions.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.5 </span>Information Collector</h3>

<div id="A4.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The information collector module was tested on 1,000 dialogues, achieving a precision of 0.84 for question relevance. The average response time was 5 seconds, with 20% of cases utilizing cached questions from the historical dialogue database.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.6 </span>Medical Specialty Selector</h3>

<div id="A4.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Medical specialty selection system input <math id="A4.SS6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{W}=\{W_{1},...,W_{n}\},n\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔚</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{W}=\{W_{1},...,W_{n}\},n\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math> is a set of <math id="A4.SS6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> medical documents <math id="A4.SS6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math>. <math id="A4.SS6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math> is a text string that contains a chat between a patient and a doctor. Medical specialty selection system output <math id="A4.SS6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{D}=[\![D_{1},...,D_{n}]\!],n\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔇</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mpadded style="width:0.108em;" width="0.108em"><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mpadded></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{D}=[\![D_{1},...,D_{n}]\!],n\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math> is a multiset of <math id="A4.SS6.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> multisets <math id="A4.SS6.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D=[\![d_{1},...,d_{k}]\!],k\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mpadded style="width:0.108em;" width="0.108em"><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mpadded></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D=[\![d_{1},...,d_{k}]\!],k\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A4.SS6.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> is a text string that contains a doctor specialty. Expectations of system performance will be shaped by the set of experts <math id="A4.SS6.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{E}=\{E_{1},...,E_{z}\},z\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔈</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{E}=\{E_{1},...,E_{z}\},z\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math>, where expert is a function <math id="A4.SS6.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E:\mathfrak{W}\mapsto\mathfrak{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>𝔚</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mi>𝔇</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E:\mathfrak{W}\mapsto\mathfrak{D}</annotation></semantics></math>. The system itself is a function <math id="A4.SS6.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A:\mathfrak{W}\mapsto\mathfrak{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>𝔚</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mi>𝔇</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A:\mathfrak{W}\mapsto\mathfrak{D}</annotation></semantics></math> which is not in a set of experts: <math id="A4.SS6.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi_{\mathfrak{E}}(A)=\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>χ</mi><mi>𝔈</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi_{\mathfrak{E}}(A)=\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math>. Then we can define the pairwise precision <math id="A4.SS6.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> and recall <math id="A4.SS6.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> between the algorithm and the expert as</p>
<table id="A4.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{AE}@k=\frac{\sum_{i=1}^{n}\mu(D^{A}_{i},D^{E}_{i})}{nk^{2}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>@</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>A</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>E</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{AE}@k=\frac{\sum_{i=1}^{n}\mu(D^{A}_{i},D^{E}_{i})}{nk^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A4.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{AE}@k=\frac{\sum_{i=1}^{n}\chi(D^{A}_{i},D^{E}_{i})}{n}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>@</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>χ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>A</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>E</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{AE}@k=\frac{\sum_{i=1}^{n}\chi(D^{A}_{i},D^{E}_{i})}{n}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS6.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A4.SS6.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{i}^{A}=A(W_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>A</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{i}^{A}=A(W_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.SS6.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{i}^{E}=E(W_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>E</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{i}^{E}=E(W_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.SS6.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> is a multiplicity function, and <math id="A4.SS6.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>χ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi</annotation></semantics></math> is a characteristic function. We consider the accuracy of the model’s answer by the complete match of its answer and the expert’s answer. Thus, we can calculate the multiplicity <math id="A4.SS6.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> and the characteristic <math id="A4.SS6.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>χ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi</annotation></semantics></math> functions in case of <math id="A4.SS6.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|D^{A}|=|D^{E}|=k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mi>A</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mi>E</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|D^{A}|=|D^{E}|=k</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A4.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu(D^{A},D^{E})=\sum_{p=1}^{k}\sum_{q=1}^{k}\begin{cases}1&amp;d^{A}_{p}=d^{E}_{q}\\
0&amp;d^{A}_{p}\neq d^{E}_{q}\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mi>A</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mi>E</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></munderover><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></munderover><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>p</mi><mi>A</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>q</mi><mi>E</mi></msubsup></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>p</mi><mi>A</mi></msubsup><mo>≠</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>q</mi><mi>E</mi></msubsup></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu(D^{A},D^{E})=\sum_{p=1}^{k}\sum_{q=1}^{k}\begin{cases}1&amp;d^{A}_{p}=d^{E}_{q}\\
0&amp;d^{A}_{p}\neq d^{E}_{q}\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS6.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A4.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi(D^{A},D^{E})=\begin{cases}1&amp;\mu(D^{A},D^{E})&gt;0\\
0&amp;\mu(D^{A},D^{E})=0\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>χ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mi>A</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mi>E</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mi>A</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mi>E</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mi>A</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mi>E</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi(D^{A},D^{E})=\begin{cases}1&amp;\mu(D^{A},D^{E})&gt;0\\
0&amp;\mu(D^{A},D^{E})=0\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS6.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The raw dataset is a collection of <math id="A4.SS6.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=360" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>360</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=360</annotation></semantics></math> chats. The first half of the dataset consists of chats from two doctors played out a pre-determined scenario. One of them knew the disease and their symptoms and was the patient. The other tried to define the disease by asking questions as the doctor. The second half of the dataset consists of the chats between the actor playing the role of a patient and CLARITY as the doctor. Ground truth labels for the dataset were marked by <math id="A4.SS6.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z=7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z=7</annotation></semantics></math> experts. Two of them are licensed doctors and other 8 are resident physicians. Each expert marked up all chats with up to <math id="A4.SS6.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{max}=5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{max}=5</annotation></semantics></math> answers. The quality metrics presented in Table <a href="#A4.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ D.6 Medical Specialty Selector ‣ Appendix D Detailed Component-Level Results ‣ CLARITY: Clinical Assistant for Routing, Inference, and Triage" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> are more than sufficient for product use. It is also interesting that the model ranks the answers in order of importance very well. The share of the first answer among the total number of correct answers is 80%, the share of the first two answers is 95%.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.T5" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 5: </span> Pairwise quality of the medical specialty selector compared to all experts. The number of specialists in the answer is equal to <math id="A4.T5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>.</figcaption>
<table id="A4.T5.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="A4.T5.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A4.T5.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_l ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><span id="A4.T5.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">k</span></th>
<th id="A4.T5.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><span id="A4.T5.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Precision@k</span></th>
<th id="A4.T5.2.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><span id="A4.T5.2.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Recall@k</span></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A4.T5.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A4.T5.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_l ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">1</th>
<td id="A4.T5.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">77<math id="A4.T5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pm" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>±</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pm</annotation></semantics></math>0.3%</td>
<td id="A4.T5.2.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">77<math id="A4.T5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pm" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>±</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pm</annotation></semantics></math>0.3%</td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T5.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A4.T5.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_l ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">2</th>
<td id="A4.T5.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">71<math id="A4.T5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pm" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>±</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pm</annotation></semantics></math>0.2%</td>
<td id="A4.T5.2.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">92<math id="A4.T5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pm" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>±</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pm</annotation></semantics></math>0.4%</td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T5.2.4" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A4.T5.2.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_b ltx_border_l ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">3</th>
<td id="A4.T5.2.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_b ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">68<math id="A4.T5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pm" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>±</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pm</annotation></semantics></math>0.3%</td>
<td id="A4.T5.2.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_b ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">96<math id="A4.T5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pm" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>±</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pm</annotation></semantics></math>0.4%</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Formal Description of the FSM</h2>

<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let the Finite State Machine be defined as 
<br class="ltx_break">a tuple <math id="A5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M=(Q,\Sigma,\Omega,C,T,\delta,\lambda,q_{0},q_{d},q_{ca},F)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M=(Q,\Sigma,\Omega,C,T,\delta,\lambda,q_{0},q_{d},q_{ca},F)</annotation></semantics></math> where:</p>
<ul id="A5.I1" class="ltx_itemize ltx_leftmargin_flush">
<li id="A5.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A5.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> is a finite set of states.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A5.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math> is the input alphabet, defined as the set of all possible strings representing user messages and previous chat history.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A5.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega</annotation></semantics></math> is the output alphabet, defined as the set of all possible text messages generated by the system.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A5.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> is the set of all conditions for transitions.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A5.I1.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> is the set of all transitions.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I1.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A5.I1.i6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta:Q\times W\rightarrow Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta:Q\times W\rightarrow Q</annotation></semantics></math> is the transition function.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I1.i7" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.i7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A5.I1.i7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda:Q\times W\rightarrow\Omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda:Q\times W\rightarrow\Omega</annotation></semantics></math> is the output function.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I1.i8" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.i8.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A5.I1.i8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{0}\in Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{0}\in Q</annotation></semantics></math> is the initial state.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I1.i9" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.i9.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A5.I1.i9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{d}\in Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{d}\in Q</annotation></semantics></math> is the default state.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I1.i10" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i10.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.i10.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A5.I1.i10.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{ca}\in Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{ca}\in Q</annotation></semantics></math> is the state with the correct answer.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I1.i11" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i11.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.i11.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A5.I1.i11.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F\subseteq Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F\subseteq Q</annotation></semantics></math> is the set of final states.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I1.i12" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i12.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.i12.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A5.I1.i12.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\_ATTEMPTS" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\_ATTEMPTS</annotation></semantics></math> is the maximum number of attempts allowed in the internal cycle.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<section id="A5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.1 </span>Set of Conditions <math id="A5.SS1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math></h3>

<div id="A5.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The set of conditions <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as:</p>
<table id="A5.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C=\{c_{1},c_{2},\ldots,c_{m}\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C=\{c_{1},c_{2},\ldots,c_{m}\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where each <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is a condition that checks if the input <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w\in W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w\in W</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies certain criteria.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.2 </span>Set of Transitions <math id="A5.SS2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math></h3>

<div id="A5.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The set of transitions <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as:</p>
<table id="A5.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=\{t_{1},t_{2},\ldots,t_{n}\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=\{t_{1},t_{2},\ldots,t_{n}\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where each <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> is a transition defined by:</p>
<table id="A5.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{j}=(q_{j},c_{j},q^{\prime}_{j})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{j}=(q_{j},c_{j},q^{\prime}_{j})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where:</p>
<ul id="A5.I2" class="ltx_itemize ltx_leftmargin_flush">
<li id="A5.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A5.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{j}\in Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{j}\in Q</annotation></semantics></math> is the source state.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A5.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{j}\subseteq C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>⊆</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{j}\subseteq C</annotation></semantics></math> is the set of conditions for the transition.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A5.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q^{\prime}_{j}\in Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q^{\prime}_{j}\in Q</annotation></semantics></math> is the target state.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Each transition <math id="A5.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> has an associated function <math id="A5.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="is\_triggered(w)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">is\_triggered(w)</annotation></semantics></math> that determines if the transition is triggered by the input <math id="A5.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w\in W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w\in W</annotation></semantics></math>. This function is defined as:</p>
<table id="A5.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{j}.is\_triggered(w)=\bigwedge_{i=1}^{|c_{j}|}c_{i}(w)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">⋀</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{j}.is\_triggered(w)=\bigwedge_{i=1}^{|c_{j}|}c_{i}(w)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.3 </span>Transition Function</h3>

<div id="A5.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The transition function <math id="A5.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as:</p>
<table id="A5.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\delta(q,w)=\left\{\begin{array}[]{ll}q^{\prime}&amp;\begin{aligned} &amp;\text{if }\exists\,t\in T:\\
&amp;\quad t.\operatorname{is\_triggered}(w)=\text{true}\end{aligned}\\[4.0pt]
q_{d}&amp;\text{otherwise}\end{array}\right." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">∃</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>is</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>triggered</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mtext>true</mtext></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mtext>otherwise</mtext></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta(q,w)=\left\{\begin{array}[]{ll}q^{\prime}&amp;\begin{aligned} &amp;\text{if }\exists\,t\in T:\\
&amp;\quad t.\operatorname{is\_triggered}(w)=\text{true}\end{aligned}\\[4.0pt]
q_{d}&amp;\text{otherwise}\end{array}\right.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">where:</p>
<ul id="A5.I3" class="ltx_itemize ltx_leftmargin_flush">
<li id="A5.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A5.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> is the set of all transitions.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A5.I3.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t.is\_triggered(w)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t.is\_triggered(w)</annotation></semantics></math> checks if the input <math id="A5.I3.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w\in W^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w\in W^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> received from the user satisfies the conditions of transition <math id="A5.I3.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.4 </span>Output Function</h3>

<div id="A5.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The output function <math id="A5.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as:</p>
<table id="A5.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda:Q\times W\rightarrow\Omega" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda:Q\times W\rightarrow\Omega</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A5.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda(q,w)=action_{q}(w)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda(q,w)=action_{q}(w)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A5.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="action_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">action_{q}</annotation></semantics></math> is the function associated with state <math id="A5.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> that generates the system response based on the input <math id="A5.SS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w\in W^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w\in W^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> received from the user.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.5 </span>External Cycle</h3>

<div id="A5.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The external cycle represents the system-user interaction sequence:</p>
<table id="A5.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(q_{i},w_{i})\vdash(q_{i+1},w_{i+1},r_{i})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊢</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(q_{i},w_{i})\vdash(q_{i+1},w_{i+1},r_{i})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where:</p>
<ul id="A5.I4" class="ltx_itemize ltx_leftmargin_flush">
<li id="A5.I4.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I4.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I4.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A5.I4.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i}\in Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}\in Q</annotation></semantics></math> is the current state.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I4.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I4.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I4.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A5.I4.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{i}\in W^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>W</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{i}\in W^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> is the input string received from the user.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I4.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I4.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I4.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A5.I4.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{i}\in\Omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{i}\in\Omega</annotation></semantics></math> is the system response.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The external cycle continues until the user interrupts it.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.6 </span>Internal Cycle</h3>

<div id="A5.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The internal cycle is defined as:</p>
<table id="A5.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(q,w)\vdash^{*}(q^{\prime},r)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mo>⊢</mo><mo>∗</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(q,w)\vdash^{*}(q^{\prime},r)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS6.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where:</p>
<ul id="A5.I5" class="ltx_itemize ltx_leftmargin_flush">
<li id="A5.I5.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I5.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I5.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A5.I5.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\vdash^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>⊢</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vdash^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> is the reflexive transitive closure of <math id="A5.I5.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\vdash" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊢</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\vdash</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I5.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I5.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I5.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A5.I5.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is the state reached after at most <math id="A5.I5.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\_ATTEMPTS" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\_ATTEMPTS</annotation></semantics></math> steps.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I5.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I5.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I5.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A5.I5.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\in\Omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\in\Omega</annotation></semantics></math> is the system response.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS6.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS6.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The internal cycle represents a single step in the external cycle, where the system generates a response based on the user input.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS7" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.7 </span>Termination Conditions</h3>

<div id="A5.SS7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The internal cycle terminates when one of the following conditions is met:</p>
<table id="A5.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\in F\lor|inner\_states|=N\_ATTEMPTS\lor q=q_{ca}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>∨</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo>∨</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\in F\lor|inner\_states|=N\_ATTEMPTS\lor q=q_{ca}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS8" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.8 </span>Output</h3>

<div id="A5.SS8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The output of the internal cycle is defined as a tuple:</p>
<table id="A5.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(r,q)\in\Omega\times Q" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(r,q)\in\Omega\times Q</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS8.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A5.SS8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> is the system response and <math id="A5.SS8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> is the next state for the external cycle.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> FSM Algorithm</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1:</span>
              
              
            <math id="alg1.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\leftarrow q_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\leftarrow q_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l1.2" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Set the initial state
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2:</span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">while</span> not user_interrupted <span id="alg1.l2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span> <span id="alg1.l2.4" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> External Cycle
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">3:</span>
              
              
              <math id="alg1.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w\leftarrow user\_input" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w\leftarrow user\_input</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l3.2" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Get the user input
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">4:</span>
              
              
              <math id="alg1.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="inner\_states\leftarrow\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">inner\_states\leftarrow\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l4.2" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Initialize the inner states list
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">5:</span>
              
              
              <span id="alg1.l5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">while</span> <math id="alg1.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\notin F\land|inner\_states|&lt;N\_ATTEMPTS\land q\neq q_{ca}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>∧</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo>∧</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\notin F\land|inner\_states|&lt;N\_ATTEMPTS\land q\neq q_{ca}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span> <span id="alg1.l5.4" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Internal Cycle
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">6:</span>
              
              
               <math id="alg1.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q^{\prime}\leftarrow\delta(q,w)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q^{\prime}\leftarrow\delta(q,w)</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l6.2" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Apply the transition function
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">7:</span>
              
              
               <math id="alg1.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\leftarrow\lambda(q^{\prime},w)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\leftarrow\lambda(q^{\prime},w)</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l7.2" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Generate the output
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">8:</span>
              
              
               <math id="alg1.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="inner\_states\leftarrow inner\_states\cup\{(q^{\prime},r)\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">inner\_states\leftarrow inner\_states\cup\{(q^{\prime},r)\}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l8.2" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Add the state-output pair to inner states
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">9:</span>
              
              
               <math id="alg1.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\leftarrow q^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\leftarrow q^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l9.2" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Update the current state
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">10:</span>
              
              
              <span id="alg1.l10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">while</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">11:</span>
              
              
              <span id="alg1.l11.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span> <math id="alg1.l11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l11.3" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Return the system response
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">12:</span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l12.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l12.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">while</span>
</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
